      "headline": "Brazilian Senator Flávio Bolsonaro leaves country for the United States after election loss",
      "body": "Brazilian Senator Flávio Bolsonaro left Brazil for the United States after losing the presidential runoff election. Incumbent President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva won a fourth term with 51.8 percent of the vote. Liberal Party leader Valdemar Costa Neto said the party accepts the election results. President Lula called the departure shameful. He said anyone who sneaks out of their country must have something to hide. Former President Jair Bolsonaro is currently serving a 27-year prison sentence for planning a coup.\n\nBrazil's Supreme Court ordered Flávio Bolsonaro to surrender his passports during a money laundering investigation. Sources said authorities cancelled his passports after he failed to surrender them within 24 hours. A police official said he did not pass through any official migration checkpoint. Todo Noticias reported he walked into Argentina before changing plans to take a private jet. But Argentinian authorities denied he entered their country. A US official confirmed entry visas would be given to him and his family. Flávio Bolsonaro has also held Italian citizenship since 2023. Investigators are looking into a 680 million pound scheme linked to betting companies.",
