      "section": "world",
      "headline": "Ceasefire holds in Russian-occupied Ukrainian city of Oleshky following international talks",
      "body": "A local ceasefire in the Russian-occupied city of Oleshky was extended across the broader Kherson region. US First Lady Melania Trump and Pope Leo XIV helped negotiate the humanitarian deal. Melania Trump led talks with civilian representatives after receiving information from UN officials. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov confirmed the truce was following plans and recognized US mediation. Ukrainian official David Arakhamia said the truce will continue until Sunday evening.\n\nBetween 1,700 and 2,000 residents remain trapped in Oleshky without food, water, or electricity. The truce allows humanitarian aid deliveries before civilian evacuations begin on Friday. Oleshky had 24,000 residents before Russian forces captured it in February 2022. Cable network Newsmax reported exclusive access to send reporters alongside observers entering the city.\n\nWhile the local truce held, fighting continued elsewhere. Russian drone and missile strikes on Kyiv killed one person and wounded 15 others overnight. Strikes in Kharkiv killed two people on Monday night. Meanwhile, leaders from Finland and Norway held a phone call with Vladimir Putin about peace talks. Denmark's prime minister criticized that call.",
